From: BRL-CAD developers <devs@brlcad.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Build both shared and static manifold; drop MANIFOLD_DEBUG

Two changes to the bext manifold build:

1. Add -DMANIFOLD_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS=ON so bext produces both
   libmanifold.so and libmanifold.a alongside the existing shared
   library.  This allows BRL-CAD's static library targets
   (BRLCAD::rt-static, etc.) to link manifold::manifold-static instead
   of falling back to the shared library, removing the runtime
   libmanifold.so dependency for consumers that link BRL-CAD statically
   (e.g. MOOSE).

   Requires the companion manifold_static_lib.patch to be applied to
   the manifold upstream first.

2. Drop -DMANIFOLD_DEBUG=ON.  Enabling debug tracing in a library
   installed as part of BRL-CAD leaks verbose timing output to end-user
   applications and results in extra debug symbols in the installed
   library.  Release builds should not carry debug instrumentation.

Applies to: BRL-CAD/bext, main branch (manifold/CMakeLists.txt)
--- a/manifold/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/manifold/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -19,7 +19,8 @@ if (ENABLE_MANIFOLD)
     CMAKE_ARGS
     ${BUILD_TYPE_SPECIFIER}
     $<$<BOOL:${CLIPPER2_TARGET}>:-DClipper2_ROOT=${CMAKE_BUNDLE_INSTALL_PREFIX}>
-    -DMANIFOLD_CBIND=OFF
-    -DMANIFOLD_DEBUG=ON
-    -DMANIFOLD_DOWNLOADS=OFF
-    -DMANIFOLD_EXPORT=OFF
-    -DMANIFOLD_JSBIND=OFF
-    -DMANIFOLD_OPTIMIZED=ON
-    -DMANIFOLD_PAR=OFF
-    -DMANIFOLD_STRICT=OFF
-    -DMANIFOLD_TEST=OFF
+    -DMANIFOLD_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS=ON
+    -DMANIFOLD_CBIND=OFF
+    -DMANIFOLD_DEBUG=OFF
+    -DMANIFOLD_DOWNLOADS=OFF
+    -DMANIFOLD_EXPORT=OFF
+    -DMANIFOLD_JSBIND=OFF
+    -DMANIFOLD_OPTIMIZED=ON
+    -DMANIFOLD_PAR=OFF
+    -DMANIFOLD_STRICT=OFF
+    -DMANIFOLD_TEST=OFF
     -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=${CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER}
